From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] tty: serial: qcom-geni: unmask the IRQ when the port suspend fails

20-sm8550/1006 masks a non-console port's IRQ before uart_suspend_port()
and unmasks it at resume. When uart_suspend_port() fails, the PM core
does not call this device's resume, so the IRQ stayed masked for good.
Unmask it on that error.

Kettle (7.3): the suspend now ends in pm_runtime_force_suspend(), so a
failure there unmasks the IRQ too.
---
diff --git a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
index 11d6163ae..801f00754 100644
--- a/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/tty/serial/qcom_geni_serial.c
@@ -2120,7 +2120,7 @@ static int qcom_geni_serial_suspend(struct device *dev)
 
 	ret = uart_suspend_port(private_data->drv, uport);
 	if (ret)
-		return ret;
+		goto err_unmask;
 
 	/*
 	 * When no_console_suspend is set the console must remain active
@@ -2129,7 +2129,18 @@ static int qcom_geni_serial_suspend(struct device *dev)
 	if (!console_suspend_enabled && uart_console(uport))
 		return 0;
 
-	return pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
+	ret = pm_runtime_force_suspend(dev);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_unmask;
+
+	return 0;
+
+err_unmask:
+	/* A failed suspend gets no resume call to unmask it. */
+	if (!uart_console(uport))
+		enable_irq(uport->irq);
+
+	return ret;
 }
 
 static int qcom_geni_serial_resume(struct device *dev)
